WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:01.543
Any 90s rom-com connoisseur

00:00:01.627 --> 00:00:03.837
knows all about
She's All That.

00:00:03.921 --> 00:00:05.380
Well, now we've welcomed

00:00:05.464 --> 00:00:08.217
its 2021
gender-swapped reimagining,

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.593
He's All That, to Netflix,

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:11.762
starring none other
than Addison Rae

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:13.931
in her debut role.
Let's dive in

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.390
to the most
searched questions

00:00:15.474 --> 00:00:16.475
about He's All That.

00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:18.727
I will create
the next prom king.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:19.728
As we mentioned,

00:00:19.811 --> 00:00:22.564
He's All That is a remake
of 90s rom-com classic,

00:00:22.648 --> 00:00:23.482
She's All That.

00:00:23.565 --> 00:00:24.816
In the original,

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.944
Freddie Prinze Jr's
popular jock, Zach,

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:29.863
is challenged to turn
artsy outsider, Laney Boggs,

00:00:29.947 --> 00:00:31.532
played
by Rachael Leigh Cook,

00:00:31.615 --> 00:00:33.659
into the most popular girl
in school.

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:38.163
The original film
boasted an impressive cast

00:00:38.247 --> 00:00:40.332
of up-and-coming actors
of the time.

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:42.292
You've got Usher,
Kieran Culkin,

00:00:42.376 --> 00:00:45.045
and eventual Oscar Winner,
Anna Paquin.

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:45.963
Laney Boggs,

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:47.589
get your cute butt
down here.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:48.966
Not to mention,

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:51.176
this was Gabrielle Union's
debut film.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.512
Oh, gracias, pappi.

00:00:53.595 --> 00:00:54.888
But did you know,

00:00:54.972 --> 00:00:56.932
the 90s film
was the modern adaptation

00:00:57.015 --> 00:00:59.226
of George Bernard Shaw's
play Pygmalion

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:02.938
and its 1964 film
counterpart, My Fair Lady.

00:01:03.021 --> 00:01:04.565
The latter, of course, being

00:01:04.648 --> 00:01:07.109
one of Audrey Hepburn's
most well-known roles.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.152
How do you do?

00:01:09.236 --> 00:01:11.196
While each of those versions
of the story

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.448
featured a young woman
being made over,

00:01:13.532 --> 00:01:15.492
He's All That
switches the script.

00:01:15.576 --> 00:01:16.410
This time,

00:01:16.493 --> 00:01:18.579
a social media influencer
is trying to turn

00:01:18.662 --> 00:01:20.372
the least popular guy
in school

00:01:20.455 --> 00:01:21.331
into prom king.

00:01:21.415 --> 00:01:24.168
And suitably,
that social media influencer

00:01:24.251 --> 00:01:26.837
is played by none other
than Addison Rae,

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.755
one of Tik Tok's
biggest stars.

00:01:28.839 --> 00:01:30.799
Addison
plays Padgett Sawyer,

00:01:30.883 --> 00:01:33.760
a girl who livestreams
every aspect of her life,

00:01:33.844 --> 00:01:36.597
unfortunately including
an embarrassing breakup

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:39.057
when she catches
her boyfriend cheating.

00:01:39.141 --> 00:01:40.350
You know what?
You don't deserve me!

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:41.476
You don't deserve my love

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:42.978
and you don't deserve
my croquembouche

00:01:43.061 --> 00:01:44.813
-you croquem-douche!
-Padgett!

00:01:44.897 --> 00:01:45.772
What?

00:01:47.566 --> 00:01:48.650
You're still live.

00:01:49.151 --> 00:01:50.944
She tries to rescue
her reputation

00:01:51.028 --> 00:01:52.863
by accepting a bet
to make-over

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.656
the least popular boy
in school.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:55.866
Don't think I can do it?

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:58.702
This is Addison's
first acting role

00:01:58.785 --> 00:01:59.620
and told Variety

00:01:59.703 --> 00:02:01.371
she started
crying hysterically

00:02:01.455 --> 00:02:03.081
when she was offered
the job.

00:02:03.165 --> 00:02:04.499
Starring opposite Addison

00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:06.460
as the 2021 version
of Laney Boggs,

00:02:06.543 --> 00:02:07.920
this time
a moody photographer

00:02:08.003 --> 00:02:10.380
named Cameron Kweller,
is Tanner Buchanan.

00:02:10.464 --> 00:02:11.590
You can't enjoy this

00:02:11.673 --> 00:02:13.509
without sharing it
with 500 strangers?

00:02:13.592 --> 00:02:16.720
500? Try 887,132.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:19.056
And we're not strangers,
they're followers.

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.141
Followers?
You mean like a cult?

00:02:21.225 --> 00:02:24.144
You may well recognise him
from Netflix's Cobra Kai,

00:02:24.228 --> 00:02:26.063
in which he plays
Johnny Lawrence's son,

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:27.064
Robby Keene.

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.023
Also appearing

00:02:28.106 --> 00:02:29.733
is The Game Plan's
Madison Pettis

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:30.651
as Alden,

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:32.861
Peyton Meyer
of Girl Meets World fame,

00:02:32.945 --> 00:02:35.113
as cheating ex
Jordan van Draanen,

00:02:35.197 --> 00:02:38.075
and singer-songwriter
Myra Molloy as Quinn.

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:39.368
You're gonna create another

00:02:39.451 --> 00:02:41.078
internationally-renowned
egomaniac?

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.955
Your eyes
weren't deceiving you

00:02:43.038 --> 00:02:44.122
when the trailer dropped.

00:02:44.206 --> 00:02:46.792
That is the one and only
Kourtney Kardashian.

00:02:47.376 --> 00:02:49.837
She plays Padgett's agent,
Jessica Miles Torres.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.755
I am your biggest supporter.

00:02:51.839 --> 00:02:54.132
No one has more faith in you
than I do,

00:02:54.216 --> 00:02:55.634
but until
you turn things around,

00:02:55.717 --> 00:02:56.552
don't talk to me.

00:02:56.635 --> 00:02:58.136
Kourtney and Adison
have been friends

00:02:58.220 --> 00:02:59.054
for a while now,

00:02:59.137 --> 00:03:02.099
appearing on each other's
social media regularly.

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:04.351
Adison told Access Hollywood
she suggested Kourtney

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:05.269
for the role,

00:03:05.352 --> 00:03:06.770
as someone
who had been important

00:03:06.854 --> 00:03:08.939
to her own journey
into stardom.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.649
-Love ya.
-Love ya.

00:03:11.733 --> 00:03:13.151
There was some speculation

00:03:13.235 --> 00:03:16.029
the characters in the 2021
film were related

00:03:16.113 --> 00:03:17.364
to the ones
from the 90s film,

00:03:17.447 --> 00:03:18.448
but that's not the case.

00:03:18.532 --> 00:03:20.576
This is
a reimagining of the story,

00:03:20.659 --> 00:03:22.202
but with
different characters.

00:03:22.286 --> 00:03:24.329
He's All That
does have some nods

00:03:24.413 --> 00:03:26.999
to the original film,
including a prom dance-off,

00:03:27.082 --> 00:03:28.750
and some familiar dialogue.

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:30.127
-I was a bet?
-No.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.837
No, I was a fucking bet.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.548
Am I a bet?
Am I a fucking bet?

00:03:34.631 --> 00:03:35.674
On top of that,

00:03:35.757 --> 00:03:38.010
two of the original
cast members return.

00:03:38.093 --> 00:03:39.970
Rachel Leigh Cook
plays Padgett's mother,

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:42.556
dispatching sage advice
for the heartbroken teen...

00:03:42.639 --> 00:03:44.850
Well, yeah, you screwed up,

00:03:45.517 --> 00:03:47.144
but it's only a mistake
if you don't learn from it.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:50.189
...and the one and only
Matthew Lillard,

00:03:50.272 --> 00:03:52.149
who played reality TV star
Brock Hudson

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.066
in She's All That,

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:54.610
returns
as the school principal.

00:03:54.693 --> 00:03:56.320
We have some
weird-ass traditions

00:03:56.403 --> 00:03:57.237
at this school.

00:03:57.321 --> 00:03:58.780
Though,
that doesn't prevent him

00:03:58.864 --> 00:04:00.073
from having a little dance.

00:04:00.157 --> 00:04:01.825
The connections
to the original

00:04:01.909 --> 00:04:02.993
don't finish there.

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:03.911
She's All That

00:04:03.994 --> 00:04:06.496
was R. Lee Fleming Jr.'s
first film to hit screens

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:07.456
and he's returned

00:04:07.539 --> 00:04:09.499
to write the script
for He's All That.

00:04:09.583 --> 00:04:10.834
Joining him
behind the screen

00:04:10.918 --> 00:04:12.336
is director Mark Waters,

00:04:12.419 --> 00:04:14.546
who definitely
knows this genre very well,

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:17.132
having directed the iconic
Mean Girls.

00:04:17.216 --> 00:04:18.759
That is so fetch.

00:04:18.842 --> 00:04:21.011
To see how the reimagining
has turned out,

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:23.847
make sure you catch it
now streaming on Netflix.

00:04:23.931 --> 00:04:26.683
And for more facts about new
and upcoming Netflix films,

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:28.227
make sure you subscribe
to the channel.

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:30.312
Why do I know this song?

